VDD_1V8 - J4 pin 7 (modem UART socket). Explicit no_connect in the schematic; board pad carries unconnected-(J4-VDD_1V8-Pad7); no track, no net. Direction CANNOT be verified: the modem module/board is not identified anywhere in the project (no part number, no datasheet, no note; socket pin names are project-defined). On cellular modules a VDD_1V8 / VDD_EXT pin is normally an OUTPUT - the module's internal 1.8 V reference for its 1.8 V I/O domain (the same domain as the socket's SDA_1V8 / SCL_1V8 / GPIO2_1V8 / ADC_1V8). If that holds, NC is correct (some datasheets still ask for a 2.2 uF cap). Status: PENDING - blocked on the module datasheet.

Modem sockets J3 (power header) + J4 (UART header), 2x12:
- Supply: the ONLY power entering the modem is 3V3_C on J4.3 (VDD_IN_UART). There is no VBAT/VCC pin on either socket. 3V3_C is fed from the ESP32 dev board's own 3V3 pins (J1.1/J1.2) - the carrier has no 3.3 V regulator for it. If the module expects a main supply, its GSM burst current (up to ~2 A for 2G, ~0.5 A Cat-M/NB) has no defined source or budget: no !padne CURRENT directive exists for J3/J4 (the E22 has one, 0.15 A).
- VDD_IN_UART tied to 3V3_C: consistent only if the pin is a host-supplied UART I/O rail input. If it is a module output, the carrier back-drives it. Verify against datasheet.
- PWR_KEY (J4.1): R15 1k to GND only - no host drive. The modem's power key is therefore hard-tied and cannot be pulsed. Acceptable only if the module auto-powers on supply; otherwise needs a GPIO/expander drive (>=500 ms pulse on most SIMCom parts).
- /PWR_EN (J3.1): driven by BOTH J1.7 (ESP32 IO7) and U8.16 (TCA9535 P13), with R16 4.7k pull-down. Two possible drivers on one net - confirm one side is input-only or split the net.
- RESET (J4.8) <- /MODEM_RST <- J1.6 (ESP32 IO6). OK. TXD/RXD (J4.4/5) <-> /UART2_MOD_RX/TX <-> J2.16/J2.17, with TP10/TP9. OK.
- SIM: neither socket carries USIM_VDD/DATA/CLK/RST/DET. The SIM socket must be on the modem board - confirm, or it is missing from the carrier.
- USB (modem firmware download): not on either socket. Confirm the modem board brings its own USB.
- Unused-by-design (explicit no_connect): J3 MIC_N/MIC_P/EAR_N/EAR_P/SDA_1V8/SCL_1V8/GPIO2_1V8/ADC_1V8; J4 VDD_1V8/GPIO1/UART_LOG_RX/UART_LOG_TX. Confirm audio, 1.8 V I2C and debug UART are intentionally unused.

